<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 17 September, from 1394 to 1978.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1394 CE <span class="tih-ago">632 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles VI orders the expulsion of the Jews from France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Charles VI decreed that all Jews must leave the kingdom of France. The edict ended organised Jewish life in most of the kingdom for some four centuries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1787 CE <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Delegates sign the US Constitution in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thirty-nine delegates signed the Constitution, creating a federal government with separated powers and checks and balances. The Bill of Rights was added by amendment in 1791.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1862 CE <span class="tih-ago">164 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Antietam, America's bloodiest single day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Union and Confederate armies suffered about 23,000 casualties along Antietam Creek in Maryland. Lee's retreat gave Lincoln the victory he needed to announce the Emancipation Proclamation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rhine" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1944 CE <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Operation Market Garden begins in the Netherlands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 35,000 Allied airborne troops landed to seize bridges leading to the Rhine. The operation failed at Arnhem, ending hopes of finishing the war by Christmas 1944.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1978 CE <span class="tih-ago">48 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Egypt and Israel sign the Camp David Accords</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After 13 days of talks hosted by Jimmy Carter, Anwar Sadat and Menachem Begin signed two frameworks for peace. They led to the Egypt-Israel peace treaty of March 1979.</p></div></li></ol>
